//             UNIT TESTING
// Unit testing is where individual componets(or "units") of an application are tested to make sure they behave as the author intended.
// These tests are usually written for a specific unit testing framework.
// It is common for these tests to get executed everytime code is committed to a project to ensure the new code does not break application functionality.
// Unit testing is just one type of testing that complex software projects may leverage.

